WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.810
1960.

2
00:00:01.860 --> 00:00:05.670
One baby is born in the
UK, and another in India.

3
00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:10.490
The UK baby could expect to
live about 71 years, on average.

4
00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:13.770
The baby born in India, about 46.

5
00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:18.730
That's a gap of about 25 years,
between two newborn babies.

6
00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:21.590
Geographers call this the development gap.

7
00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:25.750
Since 1960, has it been
closing, or getting wider?

8
00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:29.030
In this mission, you'll learn how
social development is measured,

9
00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:31.190
through health and gender.

10
00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:35.930
Then you'll read the gap over time,
and calculate how much it has changed.

11
00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:40.290
Your mission: find out whether the gap
in how long people live between rich and

12
00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:43.390
poor countries is
closing, or getting wider.
